.TH PNGFIT 1 "October 2026" "pngfit 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pngfit \- make a truecolor PNG or APNG exactly N bytes with the least visible loss
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pngfit
[\fIoptions\fR]
.B \-s
.I SIZE
.I IN.png OUT.png
.br
.B pngfit
[\fIoptions\fR]
.B \-s
.I SIZE
.B \-o
.I DIR
.IR IN.png ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pngfit
writes a standard PNG whose size is exactly
.I SIZE
bytes. It keeps the full resolution and truecolor, and gives up as little
precision as it can: PNG filter residuals are rounded to multiples of a step,
textured pixels first, flat ones last, with the byte budget spread over the image
by rate\(endistortion optimisation. The exact size comes from compressing strips of
the image independently and stitching the DEFLATE fragments into one stream, so
the file size is a plain sum that can be steered to the byte.
.PP
Animated PNGs keep every frame and every frame control. 16\-bit images are
supported. Metadata is kept by default and counted in the budget.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-size " " \fISIZE\fR
The exact output size: bytes (\fB10000000\fR), decimal units (\fB10MB\fR),
binary units (\fB10MiB\fR), or a percentage of pngfit's own lossless size
(\fB80%\fR). \fB0\fR means as small as possible. A target below what the image
can reach is not an error: pngfit warns and writes the smallest file it can make.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-max\-error " " \fIN\fR
No sample may move by more than \fIN\fR (levels of 255, or of 65535 for 16\-bit
images), whatever the size. \fB\-e 0\fR is lossless. Default: no cap, best
average quality.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-outdir " " \fIDIR\fR
Batch mode: every input is written to \fIDIR\fR under its own name. The directory is
created if it does not exist.
.TP
.BI \-\-suffix " STR"
Batch mode: \fIcover.png\fR becomes \fIcoverSTR.png\fR.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-parallel " " \fIN\fR
Batch mode: encode \fIN\fR files at once (default: as many as the threads allow).
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-strip " " \fILIST\fR
Metadata to drop, comma\-separated: \fBcolor\fR, \fBexif\fR, \fBxmp\fR,
\fBiptc\fR, \fBtext\fR, \fBphys\fR, \fBtime\fR, \fBother\fR, \fBmeta\fR (all but
colour), \fBall\fR, or chunk names such as \fBtEXt\fR. Dropping the colour profile
of a non\-sRGB image changes its colours; pngfit warns.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep " " \fILIST\fR
Keep only the listed metadata (same names, plus \fBnone\fR).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-preserve
Keep all metadata (the default).
.TP
.B \-\-alpha
Colour under fully transparent pixels is free: no bytes are spent on it. Off by
default, because some uses read colour under alpha 0.
.TP
.B \-\-lossy\-alpha
Allow rounding in the alpha channel too.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-reduce
Keep the source format even when a smaller one holds the same pixels (opaque
alpha, grey stored as colour, 16\-bit samples that are 8\-bit values).
.TP
.B \-\-fast
libdeflate level 10: on photographs about three times faster at practically the
same quality; on screenshots it costs about 2 dB.
.TP
.BI \-\-level " N"
libdeflate level for the final result, 1\(en12 (default 12).
.TP
.BI \-\-explore\-level " N"
Level for the rough part of the search on photographs (default 10).
.TP
.BI \-\-filter " N"
Base PNG filter 0\(en4 (default: probe).
.TP
.BI \-\-row\-switch " F"
A row leaves the base filter only if another is cheaper by fraction \fIF\fR
(default: probe).
.TP
.BI \-\-ladder " L"
Step ladder: \fBodd\fR (1, 3, 5, ...), \fBall\fR, or a list such as \fB1,3,5,9\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-mask " M"
Weight errors by local texture (visual masking). Off by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-strip\-rows " N"
Rows per independent strip (default: 128 for photographs, 64 for flat
synthetic images).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-thin\-strips
No thin landing strips at the bottom of the image.
.TP
.B \-\-nearest
Round every step to the nearest multiple, as pngfit 1.0 did. By default the coarse steps (9 and
up) lean towards the prediction, a dead zone that buys about 1 dB at a fifth to a third of a
photograph's lossless size; with \fB\-e\fR, or in 16\-bit images, every step is nearest anyway.
.TP
.BI \-\-rounds " N"
Rate\(endistortion refinement rounds (default 4).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Worker threads in total (default: all cores).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
No log and no progress bar.
.TP
.B \-\-json
One JSON object per file on standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-progress\-lines
Progress as machine\-readable lines on standard error
(\fB@progress\fR \fIlabel\fR TAB \fIdone\fR TAB \fItotal\fR TAB \fIseconds\fR),
for front ends such as the web page.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, including targets that could not be met (the smallest possible file
is written with a warning) and sources already within the target (left untouched,
nothing written); 1 if any file failed; 2 on a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
pngfit cover.png cover_bandcamp.png \-s 10MiB \-e 1
A 10\|485\|760\-byte cover (Bandcamp's limit) in which no pixel moved by more
than one level.
.TP
pngfit \-s 80% \-o out/ *.png
Every PNG at 80 % of its lossless size, several at once.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR oxipng (1),
.BR pngquant (1)
.SH AUTHORS
RedMoth, with Claude (Anthropic).
